<template>
    <heading>Controller</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>controller</li>
        <li>command dispatch</li>
        <li>handler stack</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>state machine</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Only the top handler decides what a command means in the current state. A child operation temporarily takes that authority; its suspended caller retains the work to perform after the child finishes. This makes a multi-step interaction a call with a continuation, rather than a collection of unrelated callbacks.</p>
        <p>Commands carry a <code>name</code> and any arguments. The same command object crosses parent/child handoffs: a child receives the command that called it, and its caller resumes with the command that completed it. Generator return values do not carry operation results; completion commands do.</p>
        <p><code>dispatch(command)</code> defers handling to a microtask so an async completion cannot re-enter a generator before it suspends. Use <code>dispatchImmediate(command)</code> when the originating user activation must reach a browser API, as with the directory picker. Handoffs within either dispatch remain synchronous.</p>
        <p><code>init(handler)</code> installs one initial, primed generator and may be called only once. Dispatch before initialization is an error. Finishing the last handler does not make the controller available for reinitialization.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>JavaScript units</name>
        <code><![CDATA[let controller = (() => {
    let handlerStack; // top of stack is current command handler

    function init(handler) {
        if (handlerStack !== undefined)
            throw new Error("Controller has already been initialized");
        handlerStack = [handler];
        result.dispatch = dispatch;
        result.dispatchImmediate = baseCommandHandler;
    }

    function dispatch(command) {
        queueMicrotask(() => baseCommandHandler(command));
    }

    function notInitialized() {
        throw new Error("Controller has not been initialized");
    }

    function baseCommandHandler(command) {
        for (let handler; (handler = handlerStack.at(-1)) !== undefined; ) {
            let result = handler.next(command);
            if (result.done)
                handlerStack.pop()
            else if (result.value === handler) // keep same handler
                return;
            else
                handlerStack.push(result.value);
        }
    }

    let result = {
        init: init,
        dispatch: notInitialized,
        dispatchImmediate: notInitialized
    };
    return result;
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
